<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		Relay-only deployment: this template intentionally OMITS the three
		keys a LAN-discovery (mDNS/Bonjour) build would need:

		  - NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription
		  - NSBonjourServices
		  - the com.apple.developer.networking.multicast entitlement (see
		    Entitlements.template.plist)

		WAN sync goes through the circuit-relay + rendezvous server (see the
		"iOS deployment" website doc), which never touches the local network
		APIs those keys gate. Adding them anyway would only cost you an
		unnecessary permission prompt on first launch, for a discovery path
		(mDNS) that is inert on-device without the multicast entitlement.

		Add NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription + NSBonjourServices back ONLY if
		you deploy a build that also does same-Wi-Fi LAN discovery (i.e. you
		went and got the multicast entitlement approved by Apple) — see the
		dioxus_fcm_sync example's info.plist for the LAN-enabled variant of
		this file, keyed on libp2p's `_p2p._udp` mDNS service type.

		dx (Dioxus CLI) 0.7+ merges this file with its generated Info.plist
		via the `ios_info_plist = "info.plist"` key in Dioxus.toml.
	-->

	<!--
		Background execution for server-initiated sync. `remote-notification`
		is what lets a silent APNs push (`content-available: 1`) wake a
		backgrounded app so it can reconnect and run a catch-up sync — the
		entire cold-/background-sync path depends on it.

		This is declared EXPLICITLY here (not left solely to dx's
		`[background] remote-notifications = true` mapping) as belt-and-braces:
		if the generated Info.plist ever ships without this key, iOS silently
		never delivers the wake push to a backgrounded app and background sync
		fails with no error and no log — the hardest failure to diagnose. dx
		merges this file with its generated plist, so an explicit entry
		guarantees the mode is present. Confirm on-device with:
		`/usr/libexec/PlistBuddy -c 'Print :UIBackgroundModes' <App>.app/Info.plist`

		`processing` / `fetch` are intentionally OMITTED: iOS does not
		guarantee opportunistic background windows, so the design relies on the
		silent-push wake, not BGTaskScheduler. Add them only if a best-effort
		BGProcessingTask top-up is introduced.
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>remote-notification</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
